course: dictionary
lesson: 2418
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, look at the words around it, which are its context. «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» Here cycle means a set of stages that happen again and again in the same order.
explain: Cycle can also be a verb. To cycle means to ride a bike, and a cycle can mean a bike. Ask yourself: is the word a thing, or something someone does? In «13 riders, 4 full tandems», the cycles are the bikes and tandems that the riders use.
explain: Context can also show a repeating pattern. «Scratching damages the skin so it itches more, the itch-scratch cycle» shows one round that starts again: scratch, itch more, scratch again. The meaning stays the same each time: something that comes round again in the same order. Swap in your meaning and check that it still makes sense.
fact: A cycle is something that happens again and again in the same order.
fact: To cycle means to ride a bike, and a cycle can also be a bike.
fact: A washing cycle is one full round of a washing machine.
fact: The life cycle of a frog or a butterfly is the set of stages it goes through, and the water cycle is how water goes up, falls as rain and goes up again.
fact: Safety tip: wear a helmet when you cycle, and use cycle lanes where they are provided.
exercise: «A butterfly's life cycle is egg, caterpillar, chrysalis and adult butterfly.» What does cycle mean here? | *Stages that happen again and again in the same order | A bike you ride to school | A loud noise from a machine | A single lap of a race track
exercise: Sam says, «I like to cycle to the park on Saturdays.» What does cycle mean here? | A pattern of numbers that repeats | A round of a washing machine | *To ride a bike | A stage in a frog's life
exercise: In «the itch-scratch cycle», what happens in each round? | Nails grow faster | *Scratching makes the itch worse, so you scratch again | The skin stops itching for good | A cut heals straight away
test: «13 riders, 4 full tandems: 4 × 2 = 8 ride tandems, 13 − 8 = 5 ride bicycles, so 4 + 5 = 9 cycles and 9 × 2 = 18 wheels.» In this sentence, what are the cycles? | *Bikes and tandems | Numbers that repeat | Stages of a life | Rounds of a machine
test: Ella learns that water goes up into the sky, falls as rain and then goes up again, over and over. Which word names this? | *Cycle | Ride | Wash | Stage
exam: «The washing cycle finished, and the clothes were clean.» In this sentence, cycle means | A repeating number pattern | *One full round of the washing machine | To ride a bike | A stage in a butterfly's life
